WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
Two French emails.

2
00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.180
One signs off «Grosses bises».

3
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.510
The other signs off «Cordialement».

4
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.230
The greetings split too.

5
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.080
«Salut !» Or «Madame, Monsieur,».

6
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.020
Or «Mesdames et Messieurs,».

7
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.120
Stranger still, one word, blog,

8
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.350
turns up in three
different families of text.

9
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.510
So why can one message
shine as a blog post,

10
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.190
yet fall flat as a formal letter?

11
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.270
In this mission, you'll see how
French texts fall into three families,

12
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.460
from diaries to speeches.

13
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.440
Then you'll build a formal
letter block by block,

14
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.890
and decide where the «Objet» line goes.

15
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.050
Your mission: work out
what turns the right words

16
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.370
into the right text.
